    },
    "version": 1,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Hi @Tim Lavelle This means all SFCC ID matching logic lives exclusively in the MRT SSR layer — no component does its own filtering. If the SSR filter is wrong (e.g. a null-ID check is missing), every page of that type is affected at once with no secondary check to catch it. Correctness of the SSR filter is load-bearing for the entire editorial rendering stack.  \n  \nYou can recheck the **MRT SSR filter (PLP example, pseudocode)** in [5.3 Data Structures / Interfaces](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/346783750/Contentful+Integration+Technical+Design+Content+Model+SFCC-249#5.3-Data-Structures-%2F-Interfaces) for the full filter logic.",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

